IRS E-file Master Concordance File
  Author:  Nonprofit Open Data Collective
  Source:  https://github.com/Nonprofit-Open-Data-Collective/irs-efile-master-concordance-file
  Docs:    https://nonprofit-open-data-collective.github.io/irs-efile-master-concordance-file/
  License: Open Data Commons Attribution License v1.0 (ODC-By-1.0), as read from
           LICENSE.md at commit d8266da934cd1cb5d1d9cedc5398ba107b0c7bbe (2026-08-23).
           Full text reproduced at data/concordance/LICENSE.md. Vendored files and
           their SHA-256s are listed in data/upstream-pins.toml.
  Use:     Primary field-to-XPath crosswalk across 990 schema versions. Every
           grant field this project extracts is located through the concordance
           rather than through XPaths written by us.

IRS-Efile-Database
  Author:  Nonprofit Open Data Collective
  Source:  https://github.com/Nonprofit-Open-Data-Collective/IRS-Efile-Database
  Docs:    https://nonprofit-open-data-collective.github.io/IRS-Efile-Database/
  License: see LICENSE at the pinned commit
  Use:     Prior art for normalized relational modeling of 990 filings. Informed
           our table decomposition and naming.

form-990-xml-mapper
  Author:  GivingTuesday (Data Commons)
  Source:  https://github.com/Giving-Tuesday/form-990-xml-mapper
  License: MIT, as read from LICENSE on the main branch (2026-09-02).
  Use:     Enumerates every XPath present in a given 990 XML schema version,
           from the IRS XSD files. The per-version inventories vendored under
           data/concordance/raw-mappings/ are this tool's output as run by the
           Nonprofit Open Data Collective; their eight columns are its eight
           columns. We use those inventories as the coverage-matrix input and
           run the tool ourselves only for schema versions they do not yet
           cover, contributing the resulting files back. XPaths present in a
           filing's schema version but absent from our concordance-derived map
           are reported, not silently dropped.

form-990-xml-parser
  Author:  GivingTuesday (Data Commons)
  Source:  https://github.com/Giving-Tuesday/form-990-xml-parser
  License: see LICENSE at the pinned commit
  Use:     Reference implementation for repeating-group traversal and schedule
           handling in 990 XML.

GivingTuesday 990 Data Commons — Form 990 Variable Dictionary and Data Mart
Dictionary
  Author:  GivingTuesday
  Source:  https://990data.givingtuesday.org/tool-repository/
  Use:     Field semantics and variable naming conventions.

open990odl
  Author:  990 Consulting, LLC
  Source:  https://github.com/990consulting/open990odl
  License: see LICENSE at the pinned commit
  Use:     Cross-reference for 990 data modeling decisions.

propublica990
  Author:  Punderthings LLC
  Source:  https://github.com/Punderthings/propublica990
  License: see LICENSE at the pinned commit
  Use:     Reference for well-behaved use of the ProPublica Nonprofit Explorer
           API.

